<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>WinExe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- The icon of the program (see tools/make-icon.py): on the exe, in the window and in the notification area. -->
    <ApplicationIcon>PingTool.ico</ApplicationIcon>
    <!-- THE version of PingTool: bump it by hand at each delivery (see pingtool-deploy.sh).
         1.0.0 = the repository as first received; 1.1.0 = after audits 451-453 (+ version system);
         1.2.0 = recent-window percentiles and jitter (PIN453.5);
         1.3.0 = TCP, HTTP and DNS probes besides ping (PIN453.6);
         1.4.0 = named monitoring profiles (PIN453.7);
         1.5.0 = network path captured at each outage (PIN453.8);
         1.5.1 = status 11004 no longer reported as "refused" (PIN453.17);
         1.5.2 = reassembly timeout no longer reported as an expired TTL (PIN453.16);
         1.5.3 = loaded settings are validated: numbers in range, clean lists (PIN453.14);
         1.5.4 = isolated successful pings are drawn on the graph (PIN453.11);
         1.5.5 = the numeric boxes are named for screen readers (PIN453.12);
         1.6.0 = the "slow" and "loss" alert thresholds are set in the window (PIN454.1);
         1.7.0 = timeline of the whole session, with a time axis (PIN454.2);
         1.7.1 = source quench no longer blamed on the destination (PIN454.5);
         1.7.2 = CSV formula protection looks at the first visible character (PIN454.6);
         1.7.3 = the screen leaves "Running" at once when every loop died (PIN454.4);
         1.8.0 = failures before "down" are set in the window, and "back up" says how long the outage lasted (PIN456.2);
         1.8.1 = the incident summary names the longest outage (PIN456.3);
         1.9.0 = optional automatic log: every ping appended to a daily CSV per host (PIN456.4);
         1.9.1 = the recent picture also shows the loss over the last 60 pings (PIN456.6);
         1.10.0 = trace route on demand from the host list, and route text shown on separate lines (PIN456.7);
         1.11.0 = command line: targets, start, minimized and interval options (PIN456.8);
         1.12.0 = profiles can be exported to a file and imported from one (PIN456.9);
         1.12.1 = export and timeline say when the log let its oldest pings go (PIN456.27);
         1.12.2 = the "Stopped" hint no longer survives a restart (PIN456.10);
         1.12.3 = full and compact window sizes follow the screen scaling (PIN456.12);
         1.12.4 = the notification icon goes away after its balloon (PIN456.13);
         1.12.5 = probes start one interval apart, whatever the answer took (PIN456.14);
         1.12.6 = the empty-address message says what to do (PIN456.15);
         1.12.7 = Enter no longer stops a run: it only starts one from the address box (PIN456.17);
         1.12.8 = the Compact box comes right after the address box in the tab order (PIN456.18);
         1.12.9 = the host list columns fit beside the scroll bar (PIN456.19);
         1.12.10 = a damaged settings file is kept aside and reported, not overwritten (PIN456.21);
         1.12.11 = a temporary DNS failure is no longer reported as an unknown name (PIN456.24);
         1.12.12 = an unreachable host has one label whether it came as an exception or as an ICMP reply (PIN456.25);
         1.12.13 = the CSV export no longer changes the line ending of the writer it is given (PIN456.28);
         1.12.14 = jitter is measured only between replies that follow each other, a loss breaks the chain (PIN456.29);
         1.13.0 = alerts can also be posted to webhooks (Slack, Discord, ntfy, JSON), and a webhook test command (PIN461.1);
         1.14.0 = a recorded log can be opened again: timeline, incidents and report (PIN461.2);
         1.15.0 = "Diagnose my connection": gateway, DNS and Internet references in one click (PIN461.3);
         1.16.0 = changes of the PC's own network are noted on the timeline and in the report (PIN461.4);
         1.17.0 = the report opens with an availability summary and a loss-by-hour grid (PIN461.5);
         1.18.0 = a name and limits of their own for each target (PIN461.6);
         1.19.0 = web targets can check the page content and warn before the certificate expires (PIN461.7);
         1.20.0 = a headless mode for scheduled runs: a duration, a report, an exit code (PIN461.8);
         1.20.1 = Enter in the address box adds the typed address before starting (PIN461.9);
         1.20.2 = the red of the diagnosis sentence reaches 4.5:1 on the dark window (PIN461.10);
         1.20.3 = PingTool has its own icon: window, notification area and exe (PIN461.11);
         1.20.4 = started minimized, the window never appears, not even for a frame (PIN461.13);
         1.20.5 = after the report is saved, say where and offer to open it (PIN461.14);
         1.20.6 = the latency graph tells a screen reader its figures (PIN461.15);
         1.20.7 = the latency graph follows a high-contrast theme (PIN461.16);
         1.20.8 = in the comparison graph each target has its own band for its lost pings (PIN461.17);
         1.20.9 = the text of the graphs is drawn with ClearType (PIN461.18);
         1.20.10 = the tab order follows the screen, left column then right column (PIN461.19, PIN461.20);
         1.20.11 = a host name cut by the narrow column shows whole on hover (PIN461.22);
         1.20.12 = the window can be resized and maximized, and remembers its size (PIN461.23);
         1.20.13 = the failures-before-down box says its unit on screen and on hover (PIN461.24);
         1.20.14 = the SVG graphs of the report have a role, a name and the figures as text (PIN461.25);
         1.20.15 = the report fits a phone: viewport, fluid graphs, wide tables scroll in their box (PIN461.26);
         1.20.16 = the report tables have header rows, column and row headings for assistive technology (PIN461.27);
         1.20.17 = settings.json tolerates trailing commas, comments and property names in any case (PIN461.28);
         1.20.18 = a target written twice in settings.json is read once (PIN461.29);
         1.20.19 = the settings file is flushed to disk before it replaces the old one, and a failed save leaves no temporary file (PIN461.30);
         1.20.20 = a value the settings reader cannot convert counts as a damaged file, kept aside, not as a locked one (PIN461.31);
         1.20.21 = the time axis labels stay right after a daylight-saving change (PIN461.32);
         1.20.22 = the dates on the time axis use the month name of the user's culture, never MM-dd (PIN461.33);
         1.21.0 = the texts of the timeline summary exist in English and French, with a table that a test keeps complete (PIN461.34);
         1.21.1 = the timeline scale follows the 98th percentile: one spike no longer flattens the chart, it is cut and marked (PIN461.35);
         1.21.2 = the timeline names the column with the most lost pings, with their count, not an isolated 1 of 1 (PIN461.36);
         1.21.3 = an outage starting at the right edge of the timeline keeps a visible band (PIN461.37);
         1.21.4 = a slowdown noticed during the first failures of an outage is no longer left ending before it starts (PIN461.38);
         1.21.5 = a second "degraded" report closes the first slowdown instead of leaving it open for ever (PIN461.39);
         1.21.6 = outages of several targets at the same time are counted once in the incident summary (PIN461.40);
         1.21.7 = the incident number of a target is a counter, not a count of the whole list (PIN461.41);
         1.21.8 = the comment of the incident number says it is counted per target and per kind (PIN461.42);
         1.21.9 = a trace whose probe cannot be sent says so, instead of blaming this PC or its link (PIN461.43);
         1.21.10 = a hop is tried up to 3 times before it is called silent: rate-limited routers no longer cut or falsify the route (PIN461.44);
         1.21.11 = a trace where nothing answers no longer concludes that the fault is on this PC (PIN461.45). -->
    <Version>1.21.11</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <EmbeddedResource Include="PingTool.ico" LogicalName="PingTool.ico" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>